  "solution": {
    "approach": "Read two decimal integers; convert the first to octal and the second to uppercase hexadecimal.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int a, b;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d\", &a, &b) == 2) {\n        printf(\"%o %X\\n\", a, b);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <iomanip>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int a, b;\n    if (cin >> a >> b) {\n        cout << oct << a << \" \" << hex << uppercase << b << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextInt()) {\n            int a = sc.nextInt();\n            int b = sc.nextInt();\n            System.out.println(Integer.toOctalString(a) + \" \" + Integer.toHexString(b).toUpperCase());\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    parts = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if len(parts) >= 2:\n        a, b = int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])\n        print(f\"{oct(a)[2:]} {hex(b)[2:].upper()}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const parts = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (parts.length >= 2) {\n        const a = parseInt(parts[0], 10).toString(8);\n        const b = parseInt(parts[1], 10).toString(16).toUpperCase();\n        console.log(`${a} ${b}`);\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Print octal using %o and uppercase hexadecimal using %X."
  },
  "hints": [
    "Use '%o' format specifier for octal representation.",
    "Use '%X' for uppercase hexadecimal representation.",
    "Separate the two representations with a space."
